## Why This Is Asked

This question probes design for per-tenant data quality and schema evolution in a large-scale streaming pipeline, focusing on data catalog lineage, backward-compatible changes, drift detection, and rollback – all essential for production data platforms.

## Key Concepts

- Streaming data quality checks (null density, ranges, referential integrity)
- Per-tenant isolation in storage and compute
- Schema evolution with backward compatibility
- End-to-end lineage via Data Catalog
- Drift detection and tenant-specific rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal validator against a registry schema (conceptual)
function validateRecord(record, schema) {
  // assume 'schema' is loaded from Data Catalog
  const valid = ajv.validate(schema, record);
  if (!valid) throw new Error('Validation error: ' + ajv.errorsText());
  return true;
}
```

