## Why This Is Asked

This question tests end-to-end real-time data engineering competencies on GCP, including multi-tenant isolation, dynamic schema evolution, data contracts, and rollback semantics, plus cross-cloud replication and testing strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time ingestion with Pub/Sub and Dataflow templates
- Per-tenant isolation using partitioned BigQuery datasets
- Central schema registry in Data Catalog for dynamic evolution
- End-to-end lineage and data contracts
- 24-hour per-tenant rollback via BigQuery time travel
- Cross-region replication to Snowflake via Snowpipe

## Code Example

```java
// Dataflow pipeline with tenant isolation and schema validation
public class TenantPipeline {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        PipelineOptions options = PipelineOptionsFactory.fromArgs(args).create();
        Pipeline pipeline = Pipeline.create(options);

        pipeline
            .apply("Read from Pub/Sub", PubsubIO.readMessagesWithAttributes()
                .fromSubscription(options.getSubscription()))
            .apply("Extract tenant ID", ParDo.of(new ExtractTenantDoFn()))
            .apply("Validate against schema", ParDo.of(new SchemaValidationDoFn()))
            .apply("Write to tenant BigQuery", new TenantBigQueryWrite());

        pipeline.run();
    }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests your ability to design a multi-tenant streaming analytics pipeline that addresses several complex requirements: cross-region data residency enforcement, privacy masking, tenant isolation, lineage tracking, rollback capabilities, schema evolution, partner data sharing, and operational observability—all working together in a unified system.

## Key Concepts
- **Pub/Sub streaming** with Dataflow for real-time processing
- **Per-tenant BigQuery** partitions with US/EU residency enforcement
- **Centralized policy engine** for consistent masking across all tenants
- **Data Catalog lineage** for governance and auditability
- **BigQuery Data Exchange** for secure cross-region partner sharing
- **24-hour rollback** via replay from Pub/Sub snapshots
- **Schema evolution** with managed schema registry
- **Observability** with retries, dead-letter queues, and alerting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: policy-based masking
function mask(record, policy) {
  const r = {...record};
  for (const field of policy.fields) {
    if (field.mask) r[field.name] = maskValue(r[field.name], field.maskType);
  }
  return r;
}

function maskValue(value, type) {
  switch (type) {
    case 'hash': return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(value).digest('hex');
    case 'redact': return '[REDACTED]';
    case 'partial': return value.slice(0, 2) + '***';
    default: return value;
  }
}
```

